      // [src_bolt_guardian_kessel2009, src_bolt_guardian_kessel2012, src_bolt_nbc_first100 | 2007-2012 | race reports + press | his own accounts] He moved from a 200 m specialist to a world-record 100 m runner within a year (NBC, Guardian 2008), and said he won in 2009 because he identified his start as the weakness and worked on it; in 2012 he again focused on his start ('I sat in the blocks a bit') and his coach told him his best race was at the end. Evidence comes mostly from his own quotations and is not independently verified as a change in method, hence modest.
